    "body": "## What\n\nMerge upstream v18.4.5 into the current fork integration branch. Retain fork build identity, CI caches, upstream approval behavior, durable subagent behavior, and Wayland/PipeWire capture.\n\n## Why\n\nUpdate the installed signed Arch package to the latest upstream release. The Wayland resolution retains dedicated window screencasts and applies upstream’s unknown-position rejection to monitor cropping. The executor retains durable-session imports alongside upstream lifecycle changes, with the obsolete interrupt-label import removed.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Source CI [#76](https://ci.n3t.work/repos/3/pipeline/76) passed for final head `86d40b5a32da034155c543e3d71e50dbe91a99de`: frozen installation, lint/format/workspace types, Rust checks, web/native/CLI builds, and exact compiled fork-version assertion.\n- Frozen local installation succeeded without scripts. Local check:ts passed formatting and early workspace checks, but timed out after 180 seconds; it is not reported as a complete pass. CI completed the full gate.\n- TS/Rust suites and worker smoke tests remain disabled under the temporary policy; checks/build success is not a test-suite pass.\n- Upstream release changelogs and attribution preserved; no additional changelog entry requested.\n- Merged source: `43cc948229429f57962c7e9d823b6c939f8d2925`; feature branch retained.\n- Arch [#195](https://ci.n3t.work/repos/2/pipeline/195) passed with source `43cc948229429f57962c7e9d823b6c939f8d2925` and recipe `22e4034acca14588d15f2b98fb9e782a00d39895`, preserving provider selections.\n- Published package and repository database signatures verified against trusted key `433D492D0438666BBB7230BB91D0A55E51016A94`. Package SHA256 matches the signed database entry.\n- Pacman upgraded only `oh-my-pi-vith-git` to `18.4.5.vith.r323.g43cc94822942-1`. PATH resolves to `/usr/bin/omp`, owned by that package, and execution reports `omp/18.4.5+vith-fork.323.43cc94822942`.\n\n---\n\n- [x] `bun check` passes\n- [ ] Tested locally\n- [ ] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)",
